[node name="Undo" type="RichTextLabel" parent="Camera3D/Interface/HelpWindow/TabContainer/Tips/ScrollContainer/VBoxContainer" unique_id=680001952]
layout_mode = 2
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[center][i]Fixing mistakes[/i][/center]
Currently, no Undo has yet been implemented. Be sure to save often! If you make a hard-to-reverse mistake, just reload the current scene with [color=#80F000]File > Reload current Project[/color]"
fit_content = true

[node name="HSeparator4" type="HSeparator" parent="Camera3D/Interface/HelpWindow/TabContainer/Tips/ScrollContainer/VBoxContainer" unique_id=47055049]
layout_mode = 2

[node name="Baseplates" type="RichTextLabel" parent="Camera3D/Interface/HelpWindow/TabContainer/Tips/ScrollContainer/VBoxContainer" unique_id=1664954887]
layout_mode = 2
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[center][i]Baseplates[/i][/center]
Using the transformation gizmo to move a [color=00C2FF]sheet[/color] down into the placement grid of its layer will set it to be a \"Baseplate\". [color=00FF97]Pins[/color] will not interact with it, meaning it doesn't need to have holes placed where non-static [color=00FF97]pins[/color] will move."
fit_content = true

[node name="HSeparator2" type="HSeparator" parent="Camera3D/Interface/HelpWindow/TabContainer/Tips/ScrollContainer/VBoxContainer" unique_id=1820618426]
layout_mode = 2

[node name="Connecting Layers" type="RichTextLabel" parent="Camera3D/Interface/HelpWindow/TabContainer/Tips/ScrollContainer/VBoxContainer" unique_id=1672251395]
layout_mode = 2
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[center][i]Connecting Layers[/i][/center]
Sometimes movements have to propagate across different layers. Global [color=00FF97]pins[/color] allow this to happen across all layers, but they may intersect sheets or the propagation is only desired across two neighboring layers. In these cases, place a regular [color=00FF97]pin[/color] in the same place in both layers, and connect the two with a [color=FF6A00]link[/color]."
fit_content = true

[node name="HSeparator3" type="HSeparator" parent="Camera3D/Interface/HelpWindow/TabContainer/Tips/ScrollContainer/VBoxContainer" unique_id=1345065729]
layout_mode = 2

[node name="Organization" type="RichTextLabel" parent="Camera3D/Interface/HelpWindow/TabContainer/Tips/ScrollContainer/VBoxContainer" unique_id=578943764]
layout_mode = 2
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[center][i]Keeping things organized[/i][/center]
For systems comprised of several subsystems, each with different numbers of layers, it is recommended to assemble these in separate project files. You can use the File>Import Machine option to instantiate saved scenes in a larger project.
Use [color=FF6A00]links[/color] to connect the interfaces of instanced machines, as by default parts of one machine do not not affect parts of another.
Instanced machines cannot be edited freely, unless Edit>Make Local is used. An exception to this is setting [color=00FF97]pins[/color] to be [color=00FFFF]outputs[/color] and their directionality/state. If the \"Store diff\" option in settings is enabled, this data, along with things like modified part positions (for example data stored in memory cells) will be saved in the project file without affecting the instance's source file.
Edit>Clear Diff can be used to reset a machine instance to its original state.

Note: At this time, importing projects that contain multiple machines will not work well."
fit_content = true

